  <!-- WHO IS IT FOR / NOT FOR -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="text-align:center;">Is a Power Flush Right for Your Wirral Property?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We give an honest check before every job. Power flushing is great but it is not right for every Wirral system.</p>

      <p style="font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:0.75rem;text-align:center;">Power flushing IS right for your Wirral home if</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:0;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Your system is more than 5 years old with signs of build-up</strong><p>Cold spots. Slow warm-up. Noisy boiler. Or rads that are barely warm. A power flush sorts these in most Wirral cases.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>You have a sealed modern system with 15mm or 22mm pipework</strong><p>Standard sealed systems in Wirral homes built after 1995 are good cases. The flush is quick and clean with our own Gas Safe heating engineers on the job.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>You have a 1975-1995 estate home with microbore pipework</strong><p>Yes. But we must use our microbore method with a chemical pre-treatment first. Tell us your home type when you call and we will confirm the approach.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>You are installing a new boiler on your existing Wirral system</strong><p>All major makers need a clean system to keep the warranty. A written report from us proves you met the rule before the new boiler is fitted.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin:1.5rem 0 0.75rem;text-align:center;">Power flushing may NOT be right if</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:0;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-no"><span class="pf-who-icon">!</span><div><strong>Your Wirral home has an open-vented gravity-fed system</strong><p>Some older Birkenhead and Wallasey homes still have gravity-fed systems. These need a different method to a sealed one. Tell us your system type when you call.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-no"><span class="pf-who-icon">!</span><div><strong>Your system has very old heavily corroded pipework</strong><p>Very old systems with rusty pipework can spring leaks. A chemical flush or a rad swap fits better in this case. We check at no cost.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-no"><span class="pf-who-icon">!</span><div><strong>Your boiler keeps losing pressure</strong><p>Pressure loss means a leak in the system. Power flushing does not seal leaks. The leak must be found and fixed first. We check this before we suggest a flush.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
