  <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="text-align:center;">What Happens During a Wirral Power Flush</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">A step-by-step view of the cleaning process we use on every Wirral job.</p>
      <div class="pf-steps" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">1</div><div><strong>System check, 20 to 30 minutes</strong><p>We check the system, look at the pipe type, scan for microbore joins, take a water sample and check the build-up level. Any worries are talked through before we start. If we think a power flush is not right for your system, we say so.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">2</div><div><strong>Chemical treatment added and system run</strong><p>For standard systems, we add a strong cleaning chemical. For microbore systems, a dispersant goes in first and works for a few hours before the machine is hooked up. This step is a must on microbore.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">3</div><div><strong>Power flush machine hooked up</strong><p>The machine is hooked up at the pump head or at a rad tail. For microbore, we use lower-velocity settings to stop the joins blocking.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">4</div><div><strong>Full system flushed in both directions</strong><p>Water is pumped through the full system in both directions. Each rad is shut off and flushed on its own. Microbore legs are flushed one at a time. The dirty water passes through the machine filter and is caught.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">5</div><div><strong>Neutraliser added. Inhibitor dosed. System balanced.</strong><p>We add neutraliser and check the pH. The system gets clean water and full-strength inhibitor. Every rad is balanced. A full heat cycle is run.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">6</div><div><strong>Written report on the day</strong><p>You get a written report on the day. It covers the date, build-up level, chemicals used and inhibitor dose. This is your warranty proof.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


